  "description": "Pins protocol::encode_head_state + protocol::decode_head_state — the MYH1 vault.head-state device-local sync baseline (§9.16). The envelope is magic (MYH1) || protocol_version (0x01) || head_format_version (0x01) || the sealed wire record (head_mac_input || head_mac) that the sibling vault-head family pins in isolation. UNIQUE among the §10.3 blob families: NOT AEAD-encrypted — the bytes are exactly the head the server already relays, and integrity is the head's own HMAC-SHA-256 under DeriveSubkey(root_key, SubkeyRole::VaultHeadMac), re-verified on load. So there is no decrypt_aead_fail shape: the MAC surface is its own distinguishable mac_fail case_kind, and the structural rejects stay under parse_fail. 9 cases: 3 encode (genesis / linear / merge) + 1 decode_ok + 1 mac_fail + 4 parse_fail. Cases generated by `cargo test -p protocol --lib emit_head_state_vectors_for_paste -- --ignored` (in protocol/src/vault_head.rs).",
